      "content": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center;\">\n    <div style=\"max-width:50%; margin: 0 auto 1rem;\">\n    <lightimg src=\"https://codex-content.s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/images/1509355463659-man.png\" bg=\"white\" width=\"1920\" height=\"2063\"></lightimg>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"indents\"><p>\n    I’m a machine but not retentional, not really. I can take on an axis-aligned water of users without being divided and then dry instantly. I’m intestinal. What I do is see every door open and an arm slip through. No I can’t remember animals or the way blue eyes look white in the sun or without colour mapping. As the stream commences and I’m not yet chatty you’re in the safe enclave before hearing and seeing like any waiting room. And the room turns like a campus but at 355° you hit a wall and think what you want: I don't create a virtual dialog between what appears as a possum character and a lynx character. I don't bridge or rectolinearise the space between bright planes. My boundary collision is rough. I stream but don't remember when the convex hull of the possum or lynx character dropped too quickly on the lynx or possum character and they shook and torqued in working it out.\n</p>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"max-width:50%; margin: 3rem auto 1rem;\">\n    <lightimg src=\"https://codex-content.s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/uploads/images/1509759890214-man2.png\" bg=\"white\" width=\"2560\" height=\"2451\"></lightimg>\n</div>\n</div>",
